course: dictionary
lesson: 15656
title: The formal word thereon
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Thereon is a formal word. You will find it in contracts, notices and old books, but people rarely use it when they talk. Its most common meaning is «on that» or «on it». The word points back to something already named in the sentence.
explain: «The sign was on the gate, and the rules were written thereon.» Thereon means the rules were written on the sign. Read the words around it to find what it points to. Then swap in «on it» and check that the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Thereon can also mean «right after that», as in «The teacher clapped twice, and thereon the room fell silent.» Here it means the room went quiet straight after the clapping. Thereupon means the same thing and is used more often.
fact: Thereon is an adverb, and it is formal and old-fashioned.
fact: «Thereon» means «on that» or «on it».
fact: «Thereon» can also mean «right after that», or «from then on».
fact: Thereon is found in contracts, notices and old books, and it points back to something already named.
fact: In everyday speech, use plain words instead: «on it» or «right after that».
exercise: «The rules were printed on the sign, and a picture of a fox was thereon.» What does thereon mean? | *On it | Far away from here | Very angry | Under the ground
exercise: «The teacher clapped twice, and thereon the room fell silent.» What does thereon mean? | Before the teacher came in | Very loudly | *Right after that | Once upon a time
exercise: A notice says: «Keep off the grass. A warning is written thereon.» Which plain words could replace thereon? | *On it | In the sea | At the train station | Yesterday morning
test: «The map was old, and a faded river was drawn thereon.» What does thereon mean? | Very quickly | Long ago | Behind it | *On it
test: «The bell rang, and thereon the children ran out to play.» What does thereon mean? | Under the desks | *Right after that | Very slowly | Far away from the school
exam: «The contract is long, and the rules thereon are very strict.» What does thereon mean? | Very quickly | *On that document | Under the bed | At the seaside
